Z||000000||Jaei Sun||03-20-2001||11:15 PM||||For those Fieros with the 2.8 v6 and the fan inside the back trunk, When does it turn on?  I have never noticed mine blowing air on the coil and alt.  Does it come on like when the radiator fan comes on or what?<P>Cuz if mine doesn't work might as well remove it along with the tubes in the engine bay... it's just dead weight.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||03-20-2001||11:35 PM||||It turns on when the radiator fan turns on.  It helps a little bit, especially with cooling off the ignition coil.  Those things don't like to get too hot.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-21-2001||09:44 AM||||If you have AC, you can test to see if it works.  Turn the car on, and turn the AC on while it is parked.  The radiator fan is supposed to come on anytime the AC is on and the car's speed is less than 35mph.  So if the rad fan's on, the coil fan should be on too.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
